    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to find a trace in logs (demo)",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 44,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "1) In **Explore \u2192 Loki**, start with:\n\n```\n{project=\"$project\",service=\"$service\"}\n```\n\n2) If your log line contains `traceId=...`, add a filter:\n\n```\n{project=\"$project\",service=\"$service\"} |= \"traceId=\"\n```\n\n3) Copy the trace id value and open **Explore \u2192 Tempo** (or click a trace link if your logs panel shows one).\n\nTip: if your service logs use a different key (`trace_id=`), search for that instead.\n"
      }
    }
